A||||9||86SE||Pics - Jeep Cherokee vs. Utility Pole - 60 MPH - I was along for the ride...||||11||
Z||000000||86SE||07-14-2001||09:16 PM||||I was in the back seat of this vehicle behind the driver.  We hit the pole after ramping a median comming out of a ditch.  We flew over 8 feet high in the air and 45 feet long.   We hit the pole 6 feet up where it snapped off.  I was the only one wearing a seatbelt and I was the only one who walked away.<P>6 Pictures - Toatal of 284k<P> <IMG SRC="http://fierodude.hypermart.net/Jeep/jeep1.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://fierodude.hypermart.net/Jeep/jeep2.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://fierodude.hypermart.net/Jeep/jeep3.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://fierodude.hypermart.net/Jeep/jeep4.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://fierodude.hypermart.net/Jeep/inside.jpg"> <P> <IMG SRC="http://fierodude.hypermart.net/Jeep/me.jpg"> ||||reg||11
Z||000001||FieroGTguy||07-14-2001||09:50 PM||||"walked away" as in survived?  Or are the other passangers recovering in a hospital?  I didn't want to ask, but it would make me feel better to know who will recover from that.<P>I hope you do physically as well as mentally.<P>Sincerely,<BR>Greg||||reg||11
Z||000002||FieroHarry||07-14-2001||09:53 PM||||I hope you guys didnt just come back from seeing "Fast and Furious".......<BR>Thats what worrys me!||||reg||1
Z||000003||CoolBlue87GT||07-14-2001||10:59 PM||||Holy crap.<P>Thank god you made it with the few scratches & bumps.  I looked at those pic & thought how could someone make it out alive.<P>Don't know if I want to drive mine after seeing this.<P>It should look like this !<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/del_now.jpg"> <BR>||||reg||4
Z||000004||baldlobo||07-15-2001||01:34 AM||||that's worse then what I did to my parents dakota. I hope the person in the co-pilot seat is ok.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||07-15-2001||02:16 AM||||Was this recent? Or a few weeks back?<BR>I remember someone on the Forum describing a similar crash.<BR>Glad you're not hurt any worse. What about the rest of the folks?<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000006||86SE||07-15-2001||02:50 AM||||There were 5 in the vehicle, everyone survived.  I did describe this accident in an earlier post, just now I have some pictures to show everyone what the vehicle looked like.<P>My friend in the passenger seat broke 3 vertebre in his back. Luckily he had his feet up on the dash because there is no room for feet, or legs in the passenger compartment.  He was airlifted to Sioux Falls where he stayed for 3 weeks.  He is in a back brace until October, but he is up and walking.  The driver was also airlifted, he broke his shoulder blade, clavicle, and cracked a few ribs, my friend in the middle broke his upper and lower jaws in 4 places and broke his right eye socket, my friend in the back seat behind the passenger broke his right arm (the force of his body weight bent the passenger seat of the brackets as you can see in the pictures).  I am the only one who remembers the accident, but I was good enough MENTALLY to go to school the next day.  I stayed in the halls for 3 hours just talking to people.<P>There is no real interior shots, but the engine is pretty much inside of the vehicle.  You can see by the one interior pic the top of the drivers seat, I knocked the head rest off the seat with my nose.<P>The accident happened May 17th at 3:45 PM, and everyone was out of the hospital by the beginning of June.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Uaana||07-15-2001||03:31 AM||||Glad to hear that you and everyone else is ok.<BR>Not to rant but I was in a rollover this last winter in a similar model Jeep I was the only one not wearing a seat belt. (rear seats suck) had to pull the driver and passenger out after I had crawled out.<BR>Just thinking if we'd been in a vehicle with a lower center of gravity we would have just spun into the snowbank instead of up and over. <BR>This is the auto my brother bought because it would be safe...<P>Again not flaming you, and really glad everone is doing fine.. just adding to my complete dislike of suv's||||reg||1
Z||000008||Fierokid87||07-15-2001||03:34 AM||||Were the others wearing thier seat belts?  I mean Obviously you were.  you walked away with less then the others did.  This goes to show though that any car in an accedent will crumple.  Not just Fiero.  Any car can be unsafe at 60 mph.<P><BR>Scott<P>------------------<BR>Fierokid's  Web site<BR>http://www.angelfire.com/sports/sfiero<P>AIM: Fierokid87<BR>ICQ: Fierokid<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sfiero.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||86SE||07-15-2001||01:21 PM||||3 weeks before this accident I was in rollover accident with one of my friends.  We were going down a gravel road at about 45 MPH when he lost control of his car, car spun around and hit the ditch backwards.  We hit dirt and flipped it right up on its top.  Wasent wearing my seatbelt then, but that taught me to wear them, but my friend dident learn from that (he is the one with the broken face).  Nobody else in the Jeep put on their seatbelts.......||||reg||1
